#N canvas 20 20 700 400 12;
#X text 20 20 t_kit -- c_kit's stand-in in a gate's scratch copy: it prints each pad and velocity it is sent as KITOUT: <pad> <velocity> \, each track's volume and pitch as KITVOL: <pad> <dB> and KITPITCH: <pad> <semitones> \, and anything else \, the effects \, as KITFX: <selector> <atoms> \, which is how sequencer-assert reads the drums c_steps plays. c_kit takes no creation arguments and has one inlet \, as this does \, and a rush-back is answered rush-at 0.1 on its second outlet \, as if a tenth of the way through the loop., f 80;
#X obj 20 120 inlet;
#X obj 20 160 route pad vol pitch;
#X obj 20 200 print KITOUT;
#X obj 150 230 print KITVOL;
#X obj 280 200 print KITPITCH;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 2 1 4 0;
#X connect 2 2 5 0;
#X obj 410 230 print KITFX;
#X connect 2 3 6 0;
#X obj 410 270 route rush-back;
#X msg 410 310 rush-at 0.1;
#X obj 410 350 outlet;
#X connect 2 3 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X obj 20 350 outlet~;
